                            <comment id="17832751" author="jueyi" created="Mon, 1 Apr 2024 07:01:23 +0000"  >&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;DevDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Dev Design&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;AddingaNewSystemConfigurationinKylinConfigBase.java&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Adding a New System Configuration in KylinConfigBase.java&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the &lt;tt&gt;KylinConfigBase.java&lt;/tt&gt; file, a new system configuration item named &lt;tt&gt;kylin.web.data-binder.auto-grow-collection-limit&lt;/tt&gt; is added. This configuration allows users to customize the size limit of arrays/lists for request parameters, with a default value of 256.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;SettingautoGrowCollectionLimitinNBasicController.java&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Setting autoGrowCollectionLimit in NBasicController.java&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the base controller &lt;tt&gt;NBasicController.java&lt;/tt&gt;, set the &lt;tt&gt;autoGrowCollectionLimit&lt;/tt&gt; to the value of the system configuration item &lt;tt&gt;kylin.web.data-binder.auto-grow-collection-limit&lt;/tt&gt;. It&apos;s important to note that setting this value too high could potentially lead to security vulnerabilities, such as OutOfMemory errors if the application is subjected to certain types of attacks (e.g., passing large arrays in the request body).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
